{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RHLW-2026-df74835ce7fd3703","published":"2026-11-24T05:05:40Z","modified":"2026-11-25T15:43:28.684325001Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-101917","CVE-2026-101918","CVE-2026-102267","CVE-2026-102268","CVE-2026-102269","CVE-2026-102270","CVE-2026-102271","CVE-2026-102274","CVE-2026-102275","CVE-2026-32597","CVE-2026-48522","CVE-2026-48523","CVE-2026-48525","CVE-2026-48526","GHSA-2gx3-rcp4-g85q","GHSA-42vr-xj54-vc7v","GHSA-752w-5fwx-jx9f","GHSA-993g-76c3-p5m4","GHSA-9v7f-9g4p-ffgj","GHSA-ffc3-869f-jxw9","GHSA-hxm8-2xgr-2p9m","GHSA-jq35-7prp-9v3f","GHSA-jwrc-g2q2-pq5p","GHSA-p4g4-x82p-q773","GHSA-w6j9-cwv2-h6wq","GHSA-w7vc-732c-9m39","GHSA-x33g-cr3x-6449","GHSA-xgmm-8j9v-c9wx"],"summary":"Lightwell Security Advisory: pyjwt 2.10.1+rhlw.1","details":"Red Hat Lightwell has released pyjwt 2.10.1+rhlw.1 with backported fixes for CVE-2026-102274, CVE-2026-102269, CVE-2026-32597, CVE-2026-101918, CVE-2026-48523, CVE-2026-101917, CVE-2026-48522, CVE-2026-102267, CVE-2026-48525, CVE-2026-102271, CVE-2026-102270, CVE-2026-102268, CVE-2026-48526, and CVE-2026-102275.\n\nCVE-2026-102274: PyJWT: Malformed RSA JWK aborts parsing of an entire JWK Set\n\nCVE-2026-102269: PyJWT: Non-canonical signature segments enable raw-token revocation bypass\n\nCVE-2026-32597: PyJWT accepts unknown `crit` header extensions (RFC 7515 §4.1.11 MUST violation)\n\nCVE-2026-101918: PyJWT: Unauthenticated RecursionError DoS in pre-verification payload parse (PyJWKClient.get_signing_key_from_jwt / verify_signature=False)\n\nCVE-2026-48523: PyJWT: Algorithm allow-list bypass when decoding with `PyJWK` / `PyJWKClient` keys\n\nCVE-2026-101917: PyJWT: PyJWKClient still amplifies unauthenticated JWKS fetches on unknown kid values (incomplete fix of CVE-2026-48524)\n\nCVE-2026-48522: PyJWKClient: missing scheme allowlist enables SSRF + token forgery via file://, ftp://, data: schemes\n\nCVE-2026-102267: PyJWT: PyJWKClient follows redirects when fetching JWKS\n\nCVE-2026-48525: PyJWT: Unauthenticated DoS via unbounded Base64URL decoding of unused payload segment in b64=false detached JWS\n\nCVE-2026-102271: PyJWT: Public keys in DER form are accepted as HMAC secrets, bypassing the CVE-2022-29217 guard\n\nCVE-2026-102270: PyJWT: ReDoS vulnerability when calling the `is_pem_format` function.\n\nCVE-2026-102268: PyJWT: Asymmetric-PEM detection bypass: whitespace/line-ending-mutated public keys skip the HS/asymmetric confusion guard\n\nCVE-2026-48526: PyJWT: Public-key JWK accepted as HMAC secret enables forged HS256 tokens when mixed families are allowed\n\nCVE-2026-102275: PyJWT accepts inconsistent OKP x/d JWKs, causing public/private key identity confusion\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for pyjwt 2.10.1 from PyPI.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"pyjwt","ecosystem":"Red Hat Lightwell:PyPI","purl":"pkg:pypi/pyjwt"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.10.1+rhlw.1"}]}],"versions":["0.1.1","0.1.2","0.1.3","0.1.4","0.1.5","0.1.6","0.1.7","0.1.8","0.1.9","0.2.0","0.2.1","0.2.3","0.3.0","0.3.1","0.3.2","0.4.0","0.4.1","0.4.2","0.4.3","1.0.0","1.0.1","1.1.0","1.3.0","1.4.0","1.4.1","1.4.2","1.5.0","1.5.1","1.5.2","1.5.3","1.6.0","1.6.1","1.6.3","1.6.4","1.7.0","1.7.1","2.0.0","2.0.0a1","2.0.0a2","2.0.1","2.1.0","2.10.0","2.10.1","2.2.0","2.3.0","2.4.0","2.5.0","2.6.0","2.7.0","2.8.0","2.9.0"],"database_specific":{"lightwell":{"backport_base_version":"2.10.1","remediated_version":"2.10.1+rhlw.1","repository_url":"https://packages.redhat.com/lightwell/python/remediated/"},"source":"https://github.com/project-lightwell/lightwell-osv/blob/main/advisories/RHLW-2026-df74835ce7fd3703.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"WEB","url":"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/releases/tag/2.14.0"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github.com/CVEProject/cvelistV5/tree/main/cves/2026/102xxx/CVE-2026-102274.json"},{"type":"ADVISORY","url":"https://github.com/jpadilla/pyjwt/security/advisories/GHSA-w6j9-cwv2-h6wq"},{"type":"ADVISORY